window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b244-cf33b7e0d94dfa18.json"]={sha256:"cf33b7e0d94dfa18535dd76862baccc7b86e0b91dfa4cc9674c61bca60a6f83a",value:{"id":"b244","title":"溢洪道消能池","titleEn":"Stilling basins for spillways","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以由水躍共軛水深連結尾水底板與消能驗證為主線，先用單寬流量與入流與福祿數與流態界定水力與構造條件，再將尾水餘量與跳躍、墩塊動量作用連結到模型比例與尺度。只採矩形明渠及局部穩態示意；消能池型式與尺寸須依完整水理及結構試驗。 每單元以原創算例、量測與失效辨識共同檢查推論。","summaryEn":"This course develops connecting hydraulic-jump depths tailwater slabs and energy-dissipation verification through Unit discharge and approach flow and Froude number and regime, then connects Tailwater margin and jump position and Baffle-block momentum action to Model ratios and scale effects. Rectangular-channel and locally steady examples do not select basin type or replace hydraulic and structural testing. Each unit combines original calculation, measurement and failure diagnosis to test the inference.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["單寬流量與入流","Unit discharge and approach flow"],["共軛水深與動量","Conjugate depth and momentum"],["尾水餘量與跳躍","Tailwater margin and jump position"],["墩塊動量作用","Baffle-block momentum action"],["模型比例與尺度","Model ratios and scale effects"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["單寬流量與入流","共軛水深與動量","尾水餘量與跳躍","墩塊動量作用","模型比例與尺度"],"labelsEn":["Unit discharge and approach flow","Conjugate depth and momentum","Tailwater margin and jump position","Baffle-block momentum action","Model ratios and scale effects"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例輸入全為教學假設，先檢查單寬流量與入流：Q=240 m3/s; width=20 m; depth=1 m; meanVelocity=240/(20*1)=12 m/s；再獨立檢查福祿數與流態：V=12 m/s; y=1 m; g=9.81 m/s2; Fr=12/sqrt(9.81*1)=3.83131 dimensionless。敏感度：流速由12增為15m/s且入流水深維持1m，福祿數由3.831增為4.789，共軛水深由4.941增為6.291m；尾水需求不隨速度線性增加。 兩個結果須按各自量綱解釋，不能直接相加或當成完整設計。只採矩形明渠及局部穩態示意；消能池型式與尺寸須依完整水理及結構試驗。 將核對採樣頻率與抗混疊設定並比較相鄰壓力感測器的相干性作為獨立驗證，明確列出尚缺的現地輸入及其對結論的影響。","textEn":"Every input in this integrated example is a teaching assumption. First examine Unit discharge and approach flow: Q=240 m3/s; width=20 m; depth=1 m; meanVelocity=240/(20*1)=12 m/s. Independently examine Froude number and regime: V=12 m/s; y=1 m; g=9.81 m/s2; Fr=12/sqrt(9.81*1)=3.83131 dimensionless. Sensitivity: increasing velocity from12 to15m/s at1m incoming depth changes Froude number from3.831 to4.789 and conjugate depth from4.941 to6.291m. Tailwater demand therefore does not scale linearly with velocity. Interpret each result in its own dimensions rather than adding them or treating them as a complete design. Rectangular-channel and locally steady examples do not select basin type or replace hydraulic and structural testing. Use the following independent check: Check sample rate and anti-alias filtering and compare coherence between adjacent pressure sensors. Identify missing field inputs and state which conclusions depend on them.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b244-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「單寬流量與入流」與「福祿數與流態」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Unit discharge and approach flow\" and \"Froude number and regime\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b244-v15-01","title":"單寬流量與入流：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Unit discharge and approach flow: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「單寬流量與入流」如何影響溢洪道消能池的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Unit discharge and approach flow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stilling basins for spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"消能池入流可能沿寬度不均，平均單寬流量只能作第一輪水力整理。槽末彎道、墩柱與收縮會讓局部速度高於平均，進而改變水躍位置與底板壓力。先核對有效過水寬及水深定義，再把全寬分布與整體流量相互核算。 驗證時應以橫向多點速度與水深積分核對總流量，並辨識以下失效情境：忽略局部高速帶會低估局部水躍與底板荷載。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「單寬流量與入流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Basin inflow may vary across the width, so mean unit discharge is an initial bookkeeping measure. Bends, piers and contraction can create local velocities above the mean and shift the jump and slab pressures. Check effective width and depth definitions, then reconcile cross-sectional distributions with total discharge. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Integrate transverse velocity and depth measurements to check total discharge. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Ignoring high-velocity strips underestimates local jump behavior and slab loading. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Unit discharge and approach flow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Q=240 m3/s; width=20 m; depth=1 m; meanVelocity=240/(20*1)=12 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Q=240 m3/s; width=20 m; depth=1 m; meanVelocity=240/(20*1)=12 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均流速可以當作整個消能池最大流速」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Mean velocity represents the maximum velocity throughout the basin\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「單寬流量與入流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Unit discharge and approach flow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-01-k1","title":"單寬流量與入流","titleEn":"Unit discharge and approach flow","text":"消能池入流可能沿寬度不均，平均單寬流量只能作第一輪水力整理。槽末彎道、墩柱與收縮會讓局部速度高於平均，進而改變水躍位置與底板壓力。","textEn":"Basin inflow may vary across the width, so mean unit discharge is an initial bookkeeping measure. Bends, piers and contraction can create local velocities above the mean and shift the jump and slab pressures.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均流速可以當作整個消能池最大流速 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Mean velocity represents the maximum velocity throughout the basin Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「單寬流量與入流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Unit discharge and approach flow\" is correct?","options":["平均流速可以當作整個消能池最大流速","消能池入流可能沿寬度不均，平均單寬流量只能作第一輪水力整理。","福祿數相同就保證全部局部壓力相同"],"optionsEn":["Mean velocity represents the maximum velocity throughout the basin","Basin inflow may vary across the width, so mean unit discharge is an initial bookkeeping measure.","Equal Froude numbers guarantee equal local pressures everywhere"],"answer":1,"explanation":"消能池入流可能沿寬度不均，平均單寬流量只能作第一輪水力整理。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Basin inflow may vary across the width, so mean unit discharge is an initial bookkeeping measure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b244-v15-02","title":"單寬流量與入流：定量估算","titleEn":"Unit discharge and approach flow: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「單寬流量與入流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Unit discharge and approach flow” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Q=240 m3/s; width=20 m; depth=1 m; meanVelocity=240/(20*1)=12 m/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Q=240 m3/s; width=20 m; depth=1 m; meanVelocity=240/(20*1)=12 m/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以橫向多點速度與水深積分核對總流量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate transverse velocity and depth measurements to check total discharge.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Q=240 m3/s; width=20 m; depth=1 m; meanVelocity=240/(20*1)=12 m/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Q=240 m3/s; width=20 m; depth=1 m; meanVelocity=240/(20*1)=12 m/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「單寬流量與入流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Unit discharge and approach flow\", which statement holds?","options":["消散的機械能會自動變成可利用電力","平均揚壓合格就排除了瞬時掀板風險","原創教學假設：Q=240 m3/s; width=20 m; depth=1 m; meanVelocity=240/(20*1)=12 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Dissipated mechanical energy automatically becomes usable electrical power","Acceptable mean uplift eliminates transient slab-lifting risk","Original teaching assumptions: Q=240 m3/s; width=20 m; depth=1 m; meanVelocity=240/(20*1)=12 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Q=240 m3/s; width=20 m; depth=1 m; meanVelocity=240/(20*1)=12 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Q=240 m3/s; width=20 m; depth=1 m; meanVelocity=240/(20*1)=12 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b244-v15-03","title":"單寬流量與入流：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Unit discharge and approach flow: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「單寬流量與入流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Unit discharge and approach flow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以橫向多點速度與水深積分核對總流量。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「忽略局部高速帶會低估局部水躍與底板荷載」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate transverse velocity and depth measurements to check total discharge. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Ignoring high-velocity strips underestimates local jump behavior and slab loading. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以橫向多點速度與水深積分核對總流量作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對忽略局部高速帶會低估局部水躍與底板荷載，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Integrate transverse velocity and depth measurements to check total discharge. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Ignoring high-velocity strips underestimates local jump behavior and slab loading. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略局部高速帶會低估局部水躍與底板荷載。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring high-velocity strips underestimates local jump behavior and slab loading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以橫向多點速度與水深積分核對總流量。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「忽略局部高速帶會低估局部水躍與底板荷載」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Integrate transverse velocity and depth measurements to check total discharge. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Ignoring high-velocity strips underestimates local jump behavior and slab loading. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以橫向多點速度與水深積分核對總流量作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對忽略局部高速帶會低估局部水躍與底板荷載，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Integrate transverse velocity and depth measurements to check total discharge. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Ignoring high-velocity strips underestimates local jump behavior and slab loading. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「單寬流量與入流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Unit discharge and approach flow\"?","options":["以橫向多點速度與水深積分核對總流量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","壓力均方根就是底板最大設計壓力"],"optionsEn":["Integrate transverse velocity and depth measurements to check total discharge.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Root-mean-square pressure equals the maximum slab design pressure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以橫向多點速度與水深積分核對總流量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate transverse velocity and depth measurements to check total discharge. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b244-v15-04","title":"單寬流量與入流：失效診斷","titleEn":"Unit discharge and approach flow: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「單寬流量與入流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Unit discharge and approach flow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略局部高速帶會低估局部水躍與底板荷載。診斷時應採取以下查核：以橫向多點速度與水深積分核對總流量，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring high-velocity strips underestimates local jump behavior and slab loading. Diagnose it by the following check: Integrate transverse velocity and depth measurements to check total discharge. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均流速可以當作整個消能池最大流速」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Mean velocity represents the maximum velocity throughout the basin\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略局部高速帶會低估局部水躍與底板荷載。診斷時應採取以下查核：以橫向多點速度與水深積分核對總流量，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Ignoring high-velocity strips underestimates local jump behavior and slab loading. Diagnose it by the following check: Integrate transverse velocity and depth measurements to check total discharge. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「單寬流量與入流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Unit discharge and approach flow\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","忽略局部高速帶會低估局部水躍與底板荷載。","福祿數相同就保證全部局部壓力相同"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Ignoring high-velocity strips underestimates local jump behavior and slab loading.","Equal Froude numbers guarantee equal local pressures everywhere"],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略局部高速帶會低估局部水躍與底板荷載。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring high-velocity strips underestimates local jump behavior and slab loading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b244-v15-05","title":"福祿數與流態：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Froude number and regime: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「福祿數與流態」如何影響溢洪道消能池的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Froude number and regime” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stilling basins for spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"福祿數比較慣性與重力作用，矩形斷面以水深作水力深度。超臨界入流需要透過水躍或其他機制轉換，但福祿數本身不能選定消能池完整構造；相同數值下，入流水層厚度、含氣量與尾水變動仍可能產生不同壓力波動。 驗證時應比較表面波傳播與實測水深速度並標示斷面形狀，並辨識以下失效情境：非矩形槽誤用總水深會算錯控制流態的水力深度。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「福祿數與流態」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Froude number compares inertia with gravity, using water depth as hydraulic depth in a rectangular section. Supercritical flow requires a transition mechanism, but the number alone does not select a complete basin design. Incoming layer thickness, aeration and tailwater variation can produce different pressure fluctuations at the same value. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare surface-wave behavior with measured depth and velocity and identify section geometry. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Using total depth in a nonrectangular channel misstates the hydraulic depth. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Froude number and regime” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：V=12 m/s; y=1 m; g=9.81 m/s2; Fr=12/sqrt(9.81*1)=3.83131 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: V=12 m/s; y=1 m; g=9.81 m/s2; Fr=12/sqrt(9.81*1)=3.83131 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「福祿數相同就保證全部局部壓力相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal Froude numbers guarantee equal local pressures everywhere\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「福祿數與流態」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Froude number and regime”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-05-k1","title":"福祿數與流態","titleEn":"Froude number and regime","text":"福祿數比較慣性與重力作用，矩形斷面以水深作水力深度。超臨界入流需要透過水躍或其他機制轉換，但福祿數本身不能選定消能池完整構造；相同數值下，入流水層厚度、含氣量與尾水變動仍可能產生不同壓力波動。","textEn":"Froude number compares inertia with gravity, using water depth as hydraulic depth in a rectangular section. Supercritical flow requires a transition mechanism, but the number alone does not select a complete basin design.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：福祿數相同就保證全部局部壓力相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal Froude numbers guarantee equal local pressures everywhere Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「福祿數與流態」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Froude number and regime\" is correct?","options":["福祿數相同就保證全部局部壓力相同","水躍前後可用機械能相等直接求水深","福祿數比較慣性與重力作用，矩形斷面以水深作水力深度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal Froude numbers guarantee equal local pressures everywhere","Equal mechanical energy determines depths across a hydraulic jump","Froude number compares inertia with gravity, using water depth as hydraulic depth in a rectangular section."],"answer":2,"explanation":"福祿數比較慣性與重力作用，矩形斷面以水深作水力深度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Froude number compares inertia with gravity, using water depth as hydraulic depth in a rectangular section. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b244-v15-06","title":"福祿數與流態：定量估算","titleEn":"Froude number and regime: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「福祿數與流態」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Froude number and regime” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：V=12 m/s; y=1 m; g=9.81 m/s2; Fr=12/sqrt(9.81*1)=3.83131 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: V=12 m/s; y=1 m; g=9.81 m/s2; Fr=12/sqrt(9.81*1)=3.83131 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較表面波傳播與實測水深速度並標示斷面形狀。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare surface-wave behavior with measured depth and velocity and identify section geometry.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：V=12 m/s; y=1 m; g=9.81 m/s2; Fr=12/sqrt(9.81*1)=3.83131 dimensionless。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: V=12 m/s; y=1 m; g=9.81 m/s2; Fr=12/sqrt(9.81*1)=3.83131 dimensionless. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「福祿數與流態」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Froude number and regime\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：V=12 m/s; y=1 m; g=9.81 m/s2; Fr=12/sqrt(9.81*1)=3.83131 dimensionless。","最大洪水必定是水躍位置最不利工況","總動量平均分攤就代表每個墩塊受力相同"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: V=12 m/s; y=1 m; g=9.81 m/s2; Fr=12/sqrt(9.81*1)=3.83131 dimensionless.","The largest flood is always the worst jump-location condition","Averaging total momentum proves equal force on every baffle"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：V=12 m/s; y=1 m; g=9.81 m/s2; Fr=12/sqrt(9.81*1)=3.83131 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: V=12 m/s; y=1 m; g=9.81 m/s2; Fr=12/sqrt(9.81*1)=3.83131 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b244-v15-07","title":"福祿數與流態：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Froude number and regime: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「福祿數與流態」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Froude number and regime” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較表面波傳播與實測水深速度並標示斷面形狀。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「非矩形槽誤用總水深會算錯控制流態的水力深度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare surface-wave behavior with measured depth and velocity and identify section geometry. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using total depth in a nonrectangular channel misstates the hydraulic depth. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較表面波傳播與實測水深速度並標示斷面形狀作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對非矩形槽誤用總水深會算錯控制流態的水力深度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare surface-wave behavior with measured depth and velocity and identify section geometry. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using total depth in a nonrectangular channel misstates the hydraulic depth. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：非矩形槽誤用總水深會算錯控制流態的水力深度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using total depth in a nonrectangular channel misstates the hydraulic depth. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較表面波傳播與實測水深速度並標示斷面形狀。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「非矩形槽誤用總水深會算錯控制流態的水力深度」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare surface-wave behavior with measured depth and velocity and identify section geometry. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using total depth in a nonrectangular channel misstates the hydraulic depth. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較表面波傳播與實測水深速度並標示斷面形狀作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對非矩形槽誤用總水深會算錯控制流態的水力深度，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare surface-wave behavior with measured depth and velocity and identify section geometry. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using total depth in a nonrectangular channel misstates the hydraulic depth. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「福祿數與流態」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Froude number and regime\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較表面波傳播與實測水深速度並標示斷面形狀。","池內殘留砂礫少就表示磨耗可以忽略"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare surface-wave behavior with measured depth and velocity and identify section geometry.","Little retained sediment means abrasion can be ignored"],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較表面波傳播與實測水深速度並標示斷面形狀。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare surface-wave behavior with measured depth and velocity and identify section geometry. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b244-v15-08","title":"福祿數與流態：失效診斷","titleEn":"Froude number and regime: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「福祿數與流態」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Froude number and regime” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"非矩形槽誤用總水深會算錯控制流態的水力深度。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較表面波傳播與實測水深速度並標示斷面形狀，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using total depth in a nonrectangular channel misstates the hydraulic depth. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare surface-wave behavior with measured depth and velocity and identify section geometry. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「福祿數相同就保證全部局部壓力相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal Froude numbers guarantee equal local pressures everywhere\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"非矩形槽誤用總水深會算錯控制流態的水力深度。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較表面波傳播與實測水深速度並標示斷面形狀，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Using total depth in a nonrectangular channel misstates the hydraulic depth. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare surface-wave behavior with measured depth and velocity and identify section geometry. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「福祿數與流態」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Froude number and regime\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","水躍前後可用機械能相等直接求水深","非矩形槽誤用總水深會算錯控制流態的水力深度。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal mechanical energy determines depths across a hydraulic jump","Using total depth in a nonrectangular channel misstates the hydraulic depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"非矩形槽誤用總水深會算錯控制流態的水力深度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using total depth in a nonrectangular channel misstates the hydraulic depth. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b244-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「共軛水深與動量」與「水躍能量損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Conjugate depth and momentum\" and \"Hydraulic jump energy loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b244-v15-09","title":"共軛水深與動量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Conjugate depth and momentum: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「共軛水深與動量」如何影響溢洪道消能池的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Conjugate depth and momentum” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stilling basins for spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"短水躍可在忽略床面摩阻且壓力近靜水的前後斷面使用動量平衡，得到共軛水深。這不是能量守恆問題，因渦流會耗散機械能；若有強烈坡度、墩塊或淹沒效應，需將外力與邊界納入，而不能硬套水平矩形公式。 驗證時應在滾流區外量測上下游水深並核對尾水是否控制跳躍，並辨識以下失效情境：在紊亂滾流內取水深會破壞靜水壓斷面的假設。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「共軛水深與動量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Across a short jump, momentum balance between approximately hydrostatic sections gives conjugate depths when bed friction is neglected. Mechanical energy is dissipated, so energy conservation cannot replace momentum. Strong slope, appurtenance forces or submergence require additional boundary terms instead of unconditional use of the horizontal rectangular formula. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure depths outside the roller and check whether tailwater controls jump position. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Sampling depth inside the turbulent roller violates the hydrostatic-section assumption. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Conjugate depth and momentum” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：y1=1 m; Fr1=12/sqrt(9.81); y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*Fr1**2)-1)=4.94130 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: y1=1 m; Fr1=12/sqrt(9.81); y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*Fr1**2)-1)=4.94130 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「水躍前後可用機械能相等直接求水深」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal mechanical energy determines depths across a hydraulic jump\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「共軛水深與動量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Conjugate depth and momentum”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-09-k1","title":"共軛水深與動量","titleEn":"Conjugate depth and momentum","text":"短水躍可在忽略床面摩阻且壓力近靜水的前後斷面使用動量平衡，得到共軛水深。這不是能量守恆問題，因渦流會耗散機械能；若有強烈坡度、墩塊或淹沒效應，需將外力與邊界納入，而不能硬套水平矩形公式。","textEn":"Across a short jump, momentum balance between approximately hydrostatic sections gives conjugate depths when bed friction is neglected. Mechanical energy is dissipated, so energy conservation cannot replace momentum.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水躍前後可用機械能相等直接求水深 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal mechanical energy determines depths across a hydraulic jump Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共軛水深與動量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Conjugate depth and momentum\" is correct?","options":["短水躍可在忽略床面摩阻且壓力近靜水的前後斷面使用動量平衡，得到共軛水深。","水躍前後可用機械能相等直接求水深","消散的機械能會自動變成可利用電力"],"optionsEn":["Across a short jump, momentum balance between approximately hydrostatic sections gives conjugate depths when bed friction is neglected.","Equal mechanical energy determines depths across a hydraulic jump","Dissipated mechanical energy automatically becomes usable electrical power"],"answer":0,"explanation":"短水躍可在忽略床面摩阻且壓力近靜水的前後斷面使用動量平衡，得到共軛水深。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Across a short jump, momentum balance between approximately hydrostatic sections gives conjugate depths when bed friction is neglected. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b244-v15-10","title":"共軛水深與動量：定量估算","titleEn":"Conjugate depth and momentum: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「共軛水深與動量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Conjugate depth and momentum” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：y1=1 m; Fr1=12/sqrt(9.81); y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*Fr1**2)-1)=4.94130 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: y1=1 m; Fr1=12/sqrt(9.81); y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*Fr1**2)-1)=4.94130 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在滾流區外量測上下游水深並核對尾水是否控制跳躍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure depths outside the roller and check whether tailwater controls jump position.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：y1=1 m; Fr1=12/sqrt(9.81); y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*Fr1**2)-1)=4.94130 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: y1=1 m; Fr1=12/sqrt(9.81); y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*Fr1**2)-1)=4.94130 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共軛水深與動量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Conjugate depth and momentum\", which statement holds?","options":["平均揚壓合格就排除了瞬時掀板風險","原創教學假設：y1=1 m; Fr1=12/sqrt(9.81); y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*Fr1**2)-1)=4.94130 m。","壓力均方根就是底板最大設計壓力"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable mean uplift eliminates transient slab-lifting risk","Original teaching assumptions: y1=1 m; Fr1=12/sqrt(9.81); y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*Fr1**2)-1)=4.94130 m.","Root-mean-square pressure equals the maximum slab design pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：y1=1 m; Fr1=12/sqrt(9.81); y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*Fr1**2)-1)=4.94130 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: y1=1 m; Fr1=12/sqrt(9.81); y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*Fr1**2)-1)=4.94130 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b244-v15-11","title":"共軛水深與動量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Conjugate depth and momentum: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「共軛水深與動量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Conjugate depth and momentum” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在滾流區外量測上下游水深並核對尾水是否控制跳躍。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「在紊亂滾流內取水深會破壞靜水壓斷面的假設」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure depths outside the roller and check whether tailwater controls jump position. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Sampling depth inside the turbulent roller violates the hydrostatic-section assumption. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以在滾流區外量測上下游水深並核對尾水是否控制跳躍作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對在紊亂滾流內取水深會破壞靜水壓斷面的假設，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure depths outside the roller and check whether tailwater controls jump position. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Sampling depth inside the turbulent roller violates the hydrostatic-section assumption. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：在紊亂滾流內取水深會破壞靜水壓斷面的假設。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sampling depth inside the turbulent roller violates the hydrostatic-section assumption. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在滾流區外量測上下游水深並核對尾水是否控制跳躍。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「在紊亂滾流內取水深會破壞靜水壓斷面的假設」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure depths outside the roller and check whether tailwater controls jump position. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Sampling depth inside the turbulent roller violates the hydrostatic-section assumption. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以在滾流區外量測上下游水深並核對尾水是否控制跳躍作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對在紊亂滾流內取水深會破壞靜水壓斷面的假設，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure depths outside the roller and check whether tailwater controls jump position. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Sampling depth inside the turbulent roller violates the hydrostatic-section assumption. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共軛水深與動量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Conjugate depth and momentum\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","福祿相似保證所有物理效應完全相似","在滾流區外量測上下游水深並核對尾水是否控制跳躍。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Froude similarity guarantees similarity of every physical effect","Measure depths outside the roller and check whether tailwater controls jump position."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在滾流區外量測上下游水深並核對尾水是否控制跳躍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure depths outside the roller and check whether tailwater controls jump position. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b244-v15-12","title":"共軛水深與動量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Conjugate depth and momentum: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「共軛水深與動量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Conjugate depth and momentum” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"在紊亂滾流內取水深會破壞靜水壓斷面的假設。診斷時應採取以下查核：在滾流區外量測上下游水深並核對尾水是否控制跳躍，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sampling depth inside the turbulent roller violates the hydrostatic-section assumption. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure depths outside the roller and check whether tailwater controls jump position. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水躍前後可用機械能相等直接求水深」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal mechanical energy determines depths across a hydraulic jump\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在紊亂滾流內取水深會破壞靜水壓斷面的假設。診斷時應採取以下查核：在滾流區外量測上下游水深並核對尾水是否控制跳躍，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Sampling depth inside the turbulent roller violates the hydrostatic-section assumption. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure depths outside the roller and check whether tailwater controls jump position. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共軛水深與動量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Conjugate depth and momentum\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["在紊亂滾流內取水深會破壞靜水壓斷面的假設。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","消散的機械能會自動變成可利用電力"],"optionsEn":["Sampling depth inside the turbulent roller violates the hydrostatic-section assumption.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Dissipated mechanical energy automatically becomes usable electrical power"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在紊亂滾流內取水深會破壞靜水壓斷面的假設。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sampling depth inside the turbulent roller violates the hydrostatic-section assumption. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b244-v15-13","title":"水躍能量損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Hydraulic jump energy loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「水躍能量損失」如何影響溢洪道消能池的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hydraulic jump energy loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stilling basins for spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"矩形水躍的能量損失取決於共軛水深差，能量主要進入大渦、紊流與含氣混合，而不是全部變成可回收功。用每單位重量的水頭損失描述，才能與上游速度水頭一致比較；不應將水頭數字直接當作功率。 驗證時應比較上下游比能與流量並確認斷面遠離滾流區，並辨識以下失效情境：把量測壓力波動當靜水深可能造成假能量增益。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水躍能量損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Energy loss in a rectangular jump depends on the conjugate-depth difference and feeds large eddies, turbulence and air mixing. Express it as head per unit weight for comparison with approach velocity head. Head is not power; conversion to an energy rate additionally requires density, gravity and discharge. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare upstream and downstream specific energy and discharge outside the roller. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Treating fluctuating pressure as hydrostatic depth can create an apparent energy gain. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hydraulic jump energy loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Conjugate depths y1=1 m,y2=5 m; headLoss=(5-1)**3/(4*1*5)=3.20 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Conjugate depths y1=1 m,y2=5 m; headLoss=(5-1)**3/(4*1*5)=3.20 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「消散的機械能會自動變成可利用電力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dissipated mechanical energy automatically becomes usable electrical power\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水躍能量損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hydraulic jump energy loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-13-k1","title":"水躍能量損失","titleEn":"Hydraulic jump energy loss","text":"矩形水躍的能量損失取決於共軛水深差，能量主要進入大渦、紊流與含氣混合，而不是全部變成可回收功。用每單位重量的水頭損失描述，才能與上游速度水頭一致比較；不應將水頭數字直接當作功率。","textEn":"Energy loss in a rectangular jump depends on the conjugate-depth difference and feeds large eddies, turbulence and air mixing. Express it as head per unit weight for comparison with approach velocity head.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：消散的機械能會自動變成可利用電力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dissipated mechanical energy automatically becomes usable electrical power Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水躍能量損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hydraulic jump energy loss\" is correct?","options":["消散的機械能會自動變成可利用電力","矩形水躍的能量損失取決於共軛水深差，能量主要進入大渦、紊流與含氣混合，而不是全部變成可回收功。","最大洪水必定是水躍位置最不利工況"],"optionsEn":["Dissipated mechanical energy automatically becomes usable electrical power","Energy loss in a rectangular jump depends on the conjugate-depth difference and feeds large eddies, turbulence and air mixing.","The largest flood is always the worst jump-location condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"矩形水躍的能量損失取決於共軛水深差，能量主要進入大渦、紊流與含氣混合，而不是全部變成可回收功。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Energy loss in a rectangular jump depends on the conjugate-depth difference and feeds large eddies, turbulence and air mixing. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b244-v15-14","title":"水躍能量損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Hydraulic jump energy loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水躍能量損失」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hydraulic jump energy loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Conjugate depths y1=1 m,y2=5 m; headLoss=(5-1)**3/(4*1*5)=3.20 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Conjugate depths y1=1 m,y2=5 m; headLoss=(5-1)**3/(4*1*5)=3.20 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較上下游比能與流量並確認斷面遠離滾流區。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare upstream and downstream specific energy and discharge outside the roller.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Conjugate depths y1=1 m,y2=5 m; headLoss=(5-1)**3/(4*1*5)=3.20 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Conjugate depths y1=1 m,y2=5 m; headLoss=(5-1)**3/(4*1*5)=3.20 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水躍能量損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hydraulic jump energy loss\", which statement holds?","options":["總動量平均分攤就代表每個墩塊受力相同","池內殘留砂礫少就表示磨耗可以忽略","原創教學假設：Conjugate depths y1=1 m,y2=5 m; headLoss=(5-1)**3/(4*1*5)=3.20 m。"],"optionsEn":["Averaging total momentum proves equal force on every baffle","Little retained sediment means abrasion can be ignored","Original teaching assumptions: Conjugate depths y1=1 m,y2=5 m; headLoss=(5-1)**3/(4*1*5)=3.20 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Conjugate depths y1=1 m,y2=5 m; headLoss=(5-1)**3/(4*1*5)=3.20 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Conjugate depths y1=1 m,y2=5 m; headLoss=(5-1)**3/(4*1*5)=3.20 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b244-v15-15","title":"水躍能量損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hydraulic jump energy loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水躍能量損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hydraulic jump energy loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較上下游比能與流量並確認斷面遠離滾流區。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把量測壓力波動當靜水深可能造成假能量增益」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare upstream and downstream specific energy and discharge outside the roller. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Treating fluctuating pressure as hydrostatic depth can create an apparent energy gain. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較上下游比能與流量並確認斷面遠離滾流區作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把量測壓力波動當靜水深可能造成假能量增益，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare upstream and downstream specific energy and discharge outside the roller. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Treating fluctuating pressure as hydrostatic depth can create an apparent energy gain. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把量測壓力波動當靜水深可能造成假能量增益。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating fluctuating pressure as hydrostatic depth can create an apparent energy gain. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較上下游比能與流量並確認斷面遠離滾流區。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把量測壓力波動當靜水深可能造成假能量增益」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare upstream and downstream specific energy and discharge outside the roller. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Treating fluctuating pressure as hydrostatic depth can create an apparent energy gain. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較上下游比能與流量並確認斷面遠離滾流區作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把量測壓力波動當靜水深可能造成假能量增益，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare upstream and downstream specific energy and discharge outside the roller. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Treating fluctuating pressure as hydrostatic depth can create an apparent energy gain. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水躍能量損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hydraulic jump energy loss\"?","options":["比較上下游比能與流量並確認斷面遠離滾流區。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","平均流速可以當作整個消能池最大流速"],"optionsEn":["Compare upstream and downstream specific energy and discharge outside the roller.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Mean velocity represents the maximum velocity throughout the basin"],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較上下游比能與流量並確認斷面遠離滾流區。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare upstream and downstream specific energy and discharge outside the roller. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b244-v15-16","title":"水躍能量損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hydraulic jump energy loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水躍能量損失」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hydraulic jump energy loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把量測壓力波動當靜水深可能造成假能量增益。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較上下游比能與流量並確認斷面遠離滾流區，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating fluctuating pressure as hydrostatic depth can create an apparent energy gain. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare upstream and downstream specific energy and discharge outside the roller. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「消散的機械能會自動變成可利用電力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dissipated mechanical energy automatically becomes usable electrical power\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把量測壓力波動當靜水深可能造成假能量增益。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較上下游比能與流量並確認斷面遠離滾流區，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Treating fluctuating pressure as hydrostatic depth can create an apparent energy gain. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare upstream and downstream specific energy and discharge outside the roller. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水躍能量損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hydraulic jump energy loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把量測壓力波動當靜水深可能造成假能量增益。","最大洪水必定是水躍位置最不利工況"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Treating fluctuating pressure as hydrostatic depth can create an apparent energy gain.","The largest flood is always the worst jump-location condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把量測壓力波動當靜水深可能造成假能量增益。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating fluctuating pressure as hydrostatic depth can create an apparent energy gain. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b244-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「尾水餘量與跳躍」與「底板揚壓與排水」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Tailwater margin and jump position\" and \"Slab uplift and drainage\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b244-v15-17","title":"尾水餘量與跳躍：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tailwater margin and jump position: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「尾水餘量與跳躍」如何影響溢洪道消能池的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tailwater margin and jump position” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stilling basins for spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"尾水不足會使水躍向下游移動甚至掃出池外，過高尾水則可能造成淹沒與不同壓力型態。比較尾水和所需共軛水深的差值有助整理工況，但不構成單一安全準則；應對洪水歷線、河床變動及下游控制進行組合試驗。 驗證時應逐一比較流量與尾水配對下的水躍位置和出池流速，並辨識以下失效情境：只測最高洪水可能漏掉中流量尾水不足的工況。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「尾水餘量與跳躍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Insufficient tailwater can move the jump downstream or sweep it out of the basin; excessive tailwater can submerge it and change pressures. The depth difference organizes operating cases but is not a universal safety criterion. Test flood hydrographs, bed changes and downstream controls in relevant combinations. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare jump location and exit velocity for paired discharge and tailwater conditions. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Testing only the largest flood can miss inadequate tailwater at intermediate discharge. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tailwater margin and jump position” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：ObservedTailwater=5.4 m; requiredConjugateDepth=5.0 m; depthMargin=5.4-5.0=0.40 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: ObservedTailwater=5.4 m; requiredConjugateDepth=5.0 m; depthMargin=5.4-5.0=0.40 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「最大洪水必定是水躍位置最不利工況」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The largest flood is always the worst jump-location condition\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「尾水餘量與跳躍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tailwater margin and jump position”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-17-k1","title":"尾水餘量與跳躍","titleEn":"Tailwater margin and jump position","text":"尾水不足會使水躍向下游移動甚至掃出池外，過高尾水則可能造成淹沒與不同壓力型態。比較尾水和所需共軛水深的差值有助整理工況，但不構成單一安全準則；應對洪水歷線、河床變動及下游控制進行組合試驗。","textEn":"Insufficient tailwater can move the jump downstream or sweep it out of the basin; excessive tailwater can submerge it and change pressures. The depth difference organizes operating cases but is not a universal safety criterion.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最大洪水必定是水躍位置最不利工況 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The largest flood is always the worst jump-location condition Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「尾水餘量與跳躍」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tailwater margin and jump position\" is correct?","options":["最大洪水必定是水躍位置最不利工況","平均揚壓合格就排除了瞬時掀板風險","尾水不足會使水躍向下游移動甚至掃出池外，過高尾水則可能造成淹沒與不同壓力型態。"],"optionsEn":["The largest flood is always the worst jump-location condition","Acceptable mean uplift eliminates transient slab-lifting risk","Insufficient tailwater can move the jump downstream or sweep it out of the basin; excessive tailwater can submerge it and change pressures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"尾水不足會使水躍向下游移動甚至掃出池外，過高尾水則可能造成淹沒與不同壓力型態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Insufficient tailwater can move the jump downstream or sweep it out of the basin; excessive tailwater can submerge it and change pressures. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b244-v15-18","title":"尾水餘量與跳躍：定量估算","titleEn":"Tailwater margin and jump position: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「尾水餘量與跳躍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tailwater margin and jump position” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：ObservedTailwater=5.4 m; requiredConjugateDepth=5.0 m; depthMargin=5.4-5.0=0.40 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: ObservedTailwater=5.4 m; requiredConjugateDepth=5.0 m; depthMargin=5.4-5.0=0.40 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐一比較流量與尾水配對下的水躍位置和出池流速。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare jump location and exit velocity for paired discharge and tailwater conditions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：ObservedTailwater=5.4 m; requiredConjugateDepth=5.0 m; depthMargin=5.4-5.0=0.40 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: ObservedTailwater=5.4 m; requiredConjugateDepth=5.0 m; depthMargin=5.4-5.0=0.40 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「尾水餘量與跳躍」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tailwater margin and jump position\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：ObservedTailwater=5.4 m; requiredConjugateDepth=5.0 m; depthMargin=5.4-5.0=0.40 m。","壓力均方根就是底板最大設計壓力","福祿相似保證所有物理效應完全相似"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: ObservedTailwater=5.4 m; requiredConjugateDepth=5.0 m; depthMargin=5.4-5.0=0.40 m.","Root-mean-square pressure equals the maximum slab design pressure","Froude similarity guarantees similarity of every physical effect"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：ObservedTailwater=5.4 m; requiredConjugateDepth=5.0 m; depthMargin=5.4-5.0=0.40 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: ObservedTailwater=5.4 m; requiredConjugateDepth=5.0 m; depthMargin=5.4-5.0=0.40 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b244-v15-19","title":"尾水餘量與跳躍：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tailwater margin and jump position: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「尾水餘量與跳躍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tailwater margin and jump position” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐一比較流量與尾水配對下的水躍位置和出池流速。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只測最高洪水可能漏掉中流量尾水不足的工況」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare jump location and exit velocity for paired discharge and tailwater conditions. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Testing only the largest flood can miss inadequate tailwater at intermediate discharge. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以逐一比較流量與尾水配對下的水躍位置和出池流速作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只測最高洪水可能漏掉中流量尾水不足的工況，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare jump location and exit velocity for paired discharge and tailwater conditions. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Testing only the largest flood can miss inadequate tailwater at intermediate discharge. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只測最高洪水可能漏掉中流量尾水不足的工況。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Testing only the largest flood can miss inadequate tailwater at intermediate discharge. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐一比較流量與尾水配對下的水躍位置和出池流速。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只測最高洪水可能漏掉中流量尾水不足的工況」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare jump location and exit velocity for paired discharge and tailwater conditions. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Testing only the largest flood can miss inadequate tailwater at intermediate discharge. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以逐一比較流量與尾水配對下的水躍位置和出池流速作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只測最高洪水可能漏掉中流量尾水不足的工況，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare jump location and exit velocity for paired discharge and tailwater conditions. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Testing only the largest flood can miss inadequate tailwater at intermediate discharge. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「尾水餘量與跳躍」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tailwater margin and jump position\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","逐一比較流量與尾水配對下的水躍位置和出池流速。","福祿數相同就保證全部局部壓力相同"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare jump location and exit velocity for paired discharge and tailwater conditions.","Equal Froude numbers guarantee equal local pressures everywhere"],"answer":1,"explanation":"逐一比較流量與尾水配對下的水躍位置和出池流速。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare jump location and exit velocity for paired discharge and tailwater conditions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b244-v15-20","title":"尾水餘量與跳躍：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tailwater margin and jump position: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「尾水餘量與跳躍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tailwater margin and jump position” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只測最高洪水可能漏掉中流量尾水不足的工況。診斷時應採取以下查核：逐一比較流量與尾水配對下的水躍位置和出池流速，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Testing only the largest flood can miss inadequate tailwater at intermediate discharge. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare jump location and exit velocity for paired discharge and tailwater conditions. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最大洪水必定是水躍位置最不利工況」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The largest flood is always the worst jump-location condition\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只測最高洪水可能漏掉中流量尾水不足的工況。診斷時應採取以下查核：逐一比較流量與尾水配對下的水躍位置和出池流速，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Testing only the largest flood can miss inadequate tailwater at intermediate discharge. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare jump location and exit velocity for paired discharge and tailwater conditions. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「尾水餘量與跳躍」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tailwater margin and jump position\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","平均揚壓合格就排除了瞬時掀板風險","只測最高洪水可能漏掉中流量尾水不足的工況。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Acceptable mean uplift eliminates transient slab-lifting risk","Testing only the largest flood can miss inadequate tailwater at intermediate discharge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只測最高洪水可能漏掉中流量尾水不足的工況。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Testing only the largest flood can miss inadequate tailwater at intermediate discharge. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b244-v15-21","title":"底板揚壓與排水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Slab uplift and drainage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「底板揚壓與排水」如何影響溢洪道消能池的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Slab uplift and drainage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stilling basins for spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"底板下滲透壓與板面脈動壓力共同決定淨向上作用，排水有效性可隨堵塞改變。以平均水頭差估揚力只處理靜態部分；接縫入壓、錨筋分配及板塊動態反應需另分析，不能用自重平衡取代完整疲勞與掀板評估。 驗證時應同步量測板面與板底壓力並檢查排水孔通暢與接縫狀態，並辨識以下失效情境：接縫高速入水可瞬間增加局部底板下壓力。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「底板揚壓與排水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Subslab pressure and fluctuating surface pressure determine net uplift, while drain effectiveness can deteriorate through blockage. An average head difference estimates only a static component. Joint pressurization, anchor load distribution and slab dynamics require separate checks; simple deadweight balance does not replace fatigue or hydraulic-jacking assessment. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure pressures above and below the slab simultaneously and inspect drains and joints. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: High-speed flow entering a joint can rapidly increase local subslab pressure. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Slab uplift and drainage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; netHead=2 m; slabArea=30 m2; uplift=1000*9.81*2*30/1000=588.6 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; netHead=2 m; slabArea=30 m2; uplift=1000*9.81*2*30/1000=588.6 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均揚壓合格就排除了瞬時掀板風險」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Acceptable mean uplift eliminates transient slab-lifting risk\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「底板揚壓與排水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Slab uplift and drainage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-21-k1","title":"底板揚壓與排水","titleEn":"Slab uplift and drainage","text":"底板下滲透壓與板面脈動壓力共同決定淨向上作用，排水有效性可隨堵塞改變。以平均水頭差估揚力只處理靜態部分；接縫入壓、錨筋分配及板塊動態反應需另分析，不能用自重平衡取代完整疲勞與掀板評估。","textEn":"Subslab pressure and fluctuating surface pressure determine net uplift, while drain effectiveness can deteriorate through blockage. An average head difference estimates only a static component.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均揚壓合格就排除了瞬時掀板風險 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Acceptable mean uplift eliminates transient slab-lifting risk Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「底板揚壓與排水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Slab uplift and drainage\" is correct?","options":["底板下滲透壓與板面脈動壓力共同決定淨向上作用，排水有效性可隨堵塞改變。","平均揚壓合格就排除了瞬時掀板風險","總動量平均分攤就代表每個墩塊受力相同"],"optionsEn":["Subslab pressure and fluctuating surface pressure determine net uplift, while drain effectiveness can deteriorate through blockage.","Acceptable mean uplift eliminates transient slab-lifting risk","Averaging total momentum proves equal force on every baffle"],"answer":0,"explanation":"底板下滲透壓與板面脈動壓力共同決定淨向上作用，排水有效性可隨堵塞改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Subslab pressure and fluctuating surface pressure determine net uplift, while drain effectiveness can deteriorate through blockage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b244-v15-22","title":"底板揚壓與排水：定量估算","titleEn":"Slab uplift and drainage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「底板揚壓與排水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Slab uplift and drainage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; netHead=2 m; slabArea=30 m2; uplift=1000*9.81*2*30/1000=588.6 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; netHead=2 m; slabArea=30 m2; uplift=1000*9.81*2*30/1000=588.6 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測板面與板底壓力並檢查排水孔通暢與接縫狀態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure pressures above and below the slab simultaneously and inspect drains and joints.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; netHead=2 m; slabArea=30 m2; uplift=1000*9.81*2*30/1000=588.6 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; netHead=2 m; slabArea=30 m2; uplift=1000*9.81*2*30/1000=588.6 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「底板揚壓與排水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Slab uplift and drainage\", which statement holds?","options":["池內殘留砂礫少就表示磨耗可以忽略","原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; netHead=2 m; slabArea=30 m2; uplift=1000*9.81*2*30/1000=588.6 kN。","平均流速可以當作整個消能池最大流速"],"optionsEn":["Little retained sediment means abrasion can be ignored","Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; netHead=2 m; slabArea=30 m2; uplift=1000*9.81*2*30/1000=588.6 kN.","Mean velocity represents the maximum velocity throughout the basin"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; netHead=2 m; slabArea=30 m2; uplift=1000*9.81*2*30/1000=588.6 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; netHead=2 m; slabArea=30 m2; uplift=1000*9.81*2*30/1000=588.6 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b244-v15-23","title":"底板揚壓與排水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Slab uplift and drainage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「底板揚壓與排水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Slab uplift and drainage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測板面與板底壓力並檢查排水孔通暢與接縫狀態。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「接縫高速入水可瞬間增加局部底板下壓力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure pressures above and below the slab simultaneously and inspect drains and joints. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: High-speed flow entering a joint can rapidly increase local subslab pressure. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以同步量測板面與板底壓力並檢查排水孔通暢與接縫狀態作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對接縫高速入水可瞬間增加局部底板下壓力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure pressures above and below the slab simultaneously and inspect drains and joints. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: High-speed flow entering a joint can rapidly increase local subslab pressure. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：接縫高速入水可瞬間增加局部底板下壓力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: High-speed flow entering a joint can rapidly increase local subslab pressure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測板面與板底壓力並檢查排水孔通暢與接縫狀態。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「接縫高速入水可瞬間增加局部底板下壓力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure pressures above and below the slab simultaneously and inspect drains and joints. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: High-speed flow entering a joint can rapidly increase local subslab pressure. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以同步量測板面與板底壓力並檢查排水孔通暢與接縫狀態作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對接縫高速入水可瞬間增加局部底板下壓力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure pressures above and below the slab simultaneously and inspect drains and joints. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: High-speed flow entering a joint can rapidly increase local subslab pressure. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「底板揚壓與排水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Slab uplift and drainage\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","水躍前後可用機械能相等直接求水深","同步量測板面與板底壓力並檢查排水孔通暢與接縫狀態。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Equal mechanical energy determines depths across a hydraulic jump","Measure pressures above and below the slab simultaneously and inspect drains and joints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步量測板面與板底壓力並檢查排水孔通暢與接縫狀態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure pressures above and below the slab simultaneously and inspect drains and joints. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b244-v15-24","title":"底板揚壓與排水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Slab uplift and drainage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「底板揚壓與排水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Slab uplift and drainage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接縫高速入水可瞬間增加局部底板下壓力。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步量測板面與板底壓力並檢查排水孔通暢與接縫狀態，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"High-speed flow entering a joint can rapidly increase local subslab pressure. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure pressures above and below the slab simultaneously and inspect drains and joints. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均揚壓合格就排除了瞬時掀板風險」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Acceptable mean uplift eliminates transient slab-lifting risk\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接縫高速入水可瞬間增加局部底板下壓力。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步量測板面與板底壓力並檢查排水孔通暢與接縫狀態，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"High-speed flow entering a joint can rapidly increase local subslab pressure. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure pressures above and below the slab simultaneously and inspect drains and joints. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「底板揚壓與排水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Slab uplift and drainage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["接縫高速入水可瞬間增加局部底板下壓力。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","總動量平均分攤就代表每個墩塊受力相同"],"optionsEn":["High-speed flow entering a joint can rapidly increase local subslab pressure.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Averaging total momentum proves equal force on every baffle"],"answer":0,"explanation":"接縫高速入水可瞬間增加局部底板下壓力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"High-speed flow entering a joint can rapidly increase local subslab pressure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b244-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「墩塊動量作用」與「脈動壓力與頻譜」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Baffle-block momentum action\" and \"Fluctuating pressure and spectrum\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b244-v15-25","title":"墩塊動量作用：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Baffle-block momentum action: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「墩塊動量作用」如何影響溢洪道消能池的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Baffle-block momentum action” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stilling basins for spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"墩塊以改變水流方向和速度承受動量作用，同時產生局部壓力脈動與渦流。集中動量估算只描述給定流束的平均作用，實際分配受旁通與三維流影響；墩塊基部、錨定與磨耗應按相同水力工況共同檢驗。 驗證時應用力計與高速水面影像核對受流範圍及作用方向，並辨識以下失效情境：流束偏移可能使單一墩塊承受遠高於平均的負荷。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「墩塊動量作用」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Baffles redirect flow and absorb momentum while generating local pressure fluctuations and vortices. A concentrated-stream estimate describes mean action for a prescribed stream, but bypass and three-dimensional flow alter distribution. Check block bases, anchorage and abrasion under consistent hydraulic conditions rather than treating force alone as sufficient. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Use force measurements and high-speed surface images to confirm intercepted flow and force direction. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A displaced jet can load one baffle far above the average. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Baffle-block momentum action” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：CapturedQ=8 m3/s; velocityChange=7 m/s; rho=1000 kg/m3; meanForce=1000*8*7/1000=56 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: CapturedQ=8 m3/s; velocityChange=7 m/s; rho=1000 kg/m3; meanForce=1000*8*7/1000=56 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「總動量平均分攤就代表每個墩塊受力相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Averaging total momentum proves equal force on every baffle\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「墩塊動量作用」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Baffle-block momentum action”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-25-k1","title":"墩塊動量作用","titleEn":"Baffle-block momentum action","text":"墩塊以改變水流方向和速度承受動量作用，同時產生局部壓力脈動與渦流。集中動量估算只描述給定流束的平均作用，實際分配受旁通與三維流影響；墩塊基部、錨定與磨耗應按相同水力工況共同檢驗。","textEn":"Baffles redirect flow and absorb momentum while generating local pressure fluctuations and vortices. A concentrated-stream estimate describes mean action for a prescribed stream, but bypass and three-dimensional flow alter distribution.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總動量平均分攤就代表每個墩塊受力相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Averaging total momentum proves equal force on every baffle Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「墩塊動量作用」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Baffle-block momentum action\" is correct?","options":["總動量平均分攤就代表每個墩塊受力相同","墩塊以改變水流方向和速度承受動量作用，同時產生局部壓力脈動與渦流。","壓力均方根就是底板最大設計壓力"],"optionsEn":["Averaging total momentum proves equal force on every baffle","Baffles redirect flow and absorb momentum while generating local pressure fluctuations and vortices.","Root-mean-square pressure equals the maximum slab design pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"墩塊以改變水流方向和速度承受動量作用，同時產生局部壓力脈動與渦流。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Baffles redirect flow and absorb momentum while generating local pressure fluctuations and vortices. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b244-v15-26","title":"墩塊動量作用：定量估算","titleEn":"Baffle-block momentum action: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「墩塊動量作用」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Baffle-block momentum action” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：CapturedQ=8 m3/s; velocityChange=7 m/s; rho=1000 kg/m3; meanForce=1000*8*7/1000=56 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: CapturedQ=8 m3/s; velocityChange=7 m/s; rho=1000 kg/m3; meanForce=1000*8*7/1000=56 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用力計與高速水面影像核對受流範圍及作用方向。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use force measurements and high-speed surface images to confirm intercepted flow and force direction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：CapturedQ=8 m3/s; velocityChange=7 m/s; rho=1000 kg/m3; meanForce=1000*8*7/1000=56 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: CapturedQ=8 m3/s; velocityChange=7 m/s; rho=1000 kg/m3; meanForce=1000*8*7/1000=56 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「墩塊動量作用」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Baffle-block momentum action\", which statement holds?","options":["福祿相似保證所有物理效應完全相似","福祿數相同就保證全部局部壓力相同","原創教學假設：CapturedQ=8 m3/s; velocityChange=7 m/s; rho=1000 kg/m3; meanForce=1000*8*7/1000=56 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Froude similarity guarantees similarity of every physical effect","Equal Froude numbers guarantee equal local pressures everywhere","Original teaching assumptions: CapturedQ=8 m3/s; velocityChange=7 m/s; rho=1000 kg/m3; meanForce=1000*8*7/1000=56 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：CapturedQ=8 m3/s; velocityChange=7 m/s; rho=1000 kg/m3; meanForce=1000*8*7/1000=56 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: CapturedQ=8 m3/s; velocityChange=7 m/s; rho=1000 kg/m3; meanForce=1000*8*7/1000=56 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b244-v15-27","title":"墩塊動量作用：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Baffle-block momentum action: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「墩塊動量作用」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Baffle-block momentum action” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用力計與高速水面影像核對受流範圍及作用方向。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「流束偏移可能使單一墩塊承受遠高於平均的負荷」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use force measurements and high-speed surface images to confirm intercepted flow and force direction. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A displaced jet can load one baffle far above the average. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以用力計與高速水面影像核對受流範圍及作用方向作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對流束偏移可能使單一墩塊承受遠高於平均的負荷，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use force measurements and high-speed surface images to confirm intercepted flow and force direction. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A displaced jet can load one baffle far above the average. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：流束偏移可能使單一墩塊承受遠高於平均的負荷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A displaced jet can load one baffle far above the average. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用力計與高速水面影像核對受流範圍及作用方向。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「流束偏移可能使單一墩塊承受遠高於平均的負荷」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Use force measurements and high-speed surface images to confirm intercepted flow and force direction. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A displaced jet can load one baffle far above the average. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以用力計與高速水面影像核對受流範圍及作用方向作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對流束偏移可能使單一墩塊承受遠高於平均的負荷，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use force measurements and high-speed surface images to confirm intercepted flow and force direction. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A displaced jet can load one baffle far above the average. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「墩塊動量作用」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Baffle-block momentum action\"?","options":["用力計與高速水面影像核對受流範圍及作用方向。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","消散的機械能會自動變成可利用電力"],"optionsEn":["Use force measurements and high-speed surface images to confirm intercepted flow and force direction.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Dissipated mechanical energy automatically becomes usable electrical power"],"answer":0,"explanation":"用力計與高速水面影像核對受流範圍及作用方向。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use force measurements and high-speed surface images to confirm intercepted flow and force direction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b244-v15-28","title":"墩塊動量作用：失效診斷","titleEn":"Baffle-block momentum action: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「墩塊動量作用」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Baffle-block momentum action” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"流束偏移可能使單一墩塊承受遠高於平均的負荷。診斷時應採取以下查核：用力計與高速水面影像核對受流範圍及作用方向，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A displaced jet can load one baffle far above the average. Diagnose it by the following check: Use force measurements and high-speed surface images to confirm intercepted flow and force direction. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總動量平均分攤就代表每個墩塊受力相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Averaging total momentum proves equal force on every baffle\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"流束偏移可能使單一墩塊承受遠高於平均的負荷。診斷時應採取以下查核：用力計與高速水面影像核對受流範圍及作用方向，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A displaced jet can load one baffle far above the average. Diagnose it by the following check: Use force measurements and high-speed surface images to confirm intercepted flow and force direction. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「墩塊動量作用」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Baffle-block momentum action\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","流束偏移可能使單一墩塊承受遠高於平均的負荷。","壓力均方根就是底板最大設計壓力"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A displaced jet can load one baffle far above the average.","Root-mean-square pressure equals the maximum slab design pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"流束偏移可能使單一墩塊承受遠高於平均的負荷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A displaced jet can load one baffle far above the average. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b244-v15-29","title":"脈動壓力與頻譜：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fluctuating pressure and spectrum: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「脈動壓力與頻譜」如何影響溢洪道消能池的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fluctuating pressure and spectrum” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stilling basins for spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"紊流壓力的均方根反映波動強度，但極值與持續時間還依頻譜、空間相關與採樣率而異。單點量測不能直接代表整塊底板合力；應建立多點同步紀錄，分辨結構共振附近的頻率與一般寬頻湍流。 驗證時應核對採樣頻率與抗混疊設定並比較相鄰壓力感測器的相干性，並辨識以下失效情境：採樣過慢可把高頻壓力錯折成假的低頻共振。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「脈動壓力與頻譜」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pressure RMS describes fluctuation intensity, while extremes and duration depend on spectrum, spatial correlation and sampling. One sensor does not define the resultant on a whole slab. Use synchronized arrays to distinguish excitation near structural resonance from broader turbulence and preserve the observation duration used for statistics. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check sample rate and anti-alias filtering and compare coherence between adjacent pressure sensors. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Slow sampling can alias high-frequency pressure into false low-frequency resonance. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fluctuating pressure and spectrum” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Zero-mean samples=-6,0,6 kPa; RMS=sqrt((36+0+36)/3)=4.89898 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Zero-mean samples=-6,0,6 kPa; RMS=sqrt((36+0+36)/3)=4.89898 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「壓力均方根就是底板最大設計壓力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Root-mean-square pressure equals the maximum slab design pressure\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「脈動壓力與頻譜」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fluctuating pressure and spectrum”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-29-k1","title":"脈動壓力與頻譜","titleEn":"Fluctuating pressure and spectrum","text":"紊流壓力的均方根反映波動強度，但極值與持續時間還依頻譜、空間相關與採樣率而異。單點量測不能直接代表整塊底板合力；應建立多點同步紀錄，分辨結構共振附近的頻率與一般寬頻湍流。","textEn":"Pressure RMS describes fluctuation intensity, while extremes and duration depend on spectrum, spatial correlation and sampling. One sensor does not define the resultant on a whole slab.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：壓力均方根就是底板最大設計壓力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Root-mean-square pressure equals the maximum slab design pressure Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「脈動壓力與頻譜」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fluctuating pressure and spectrum\" is correct?","options":["壓力均方根就是底板最大設計壓力","池內殘留砂礫少就表示磨耗可以忽略","紊流壓力的均方根反映波動強度，但極值與持續時間還依頻譜、空間相關與採樣率而異。"],"optionsEn":["Root-mean-square pressure equals the maximum slab design pressure","Little retained sediment means abrasion can be ignored","Pressure RMS describes fluctuation intensity, while extremes and duration depend on spectrum, spatial correlation and sampling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"紊流壓力的均方根反映波動強度，但極值與持續時間還依頻譜、空間相關與採樣率而異。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pressure RMS describes fluctuation intensity, while extremes and duration depend on spectrum, spatial correlation and sampling. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b244-v15-30","title":"脈動壓力與頻譜：定量估算","titleEn":"Fluctuating pressure and spectrum: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「脈動壓力與頻譜」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fluctuating pressure and spectrum” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Zero-mean samples=-6,0,6 kPa; RMS=sqrt((36+0+36)/3)=4.89898 kPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Zero-mean samples=-6,0,6 kPa; RMS=sqrt((36+0+36)/3)=4.89898 kPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對採樣頻率與抗混疊設定並比較相鄰壓力感測器的相干性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check sample rate and anti-alias filtering and compare coherence between adjacent pressure sensors.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Zero-mean samples=-6,0,6 kPa; RMS=sqrt((36+0+36)/3)=4.89898 kPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Zero-mean samples=-6,0,6 kPa; RMS=sqrt((36+0+36)/3)=4.89898 kPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「脈動壓力與頻譜」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fluctuating pressure and spectrum\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Zero-mean samples=-6,0,6 kPa; RMS=sqrt((36+0+36)/3)=4.89898 kPa。","平均流速可以當作整個消能池最大流速","水躍前後可用機械能相等直接求水深"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Zero-mean samples=-6,0,6 kPa; RMS=sqrt((36+0+36)/3)=4.89898 kPa.","Mean velocity represents the maximum velocity throughout the basin","Equal mechanical energy determines depths across a hydraulic jump"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Zero-mean samples=-6,0,6 kPa; RMS=sqrt((36+0+36)/3)=4.89898 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Zero-mean samples=-6,0,6 kPa; RMS=sqrt((36+0+36)/3)=4.89898 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b244-v15-31","title":"脈動壓力與頻譜：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fluctuating pressure and spectrum: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「脈動壓力與頻譜」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fluctuating pressure and spectrum” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對採樣頻率與抗混疊設定並比較相鄰壓力感測器的相干性。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「採樣過慢可把高頻壓力錯折成假的低頻共振」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check sample rate and anti-alias filtering and compare coherence between adjacent pressure sensors. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Slow sampling can alias high-frequency pressure into false low-frequency resonance. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以核對採樣頻率與抗混疊設定並比較相鄰壓力感測器的相干性作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對採樣過慢可把高頻壓力錯折成假的低頻共振，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check sample rate and anti-alias filtering and compare coherence between adjacent pressure sensors. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Slow sampling can alias high-frequency pressure into false low-frequency resonance. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：採樣過慢可把高頻壓力錯折成假的低頻共振。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Slow sampling can alias high-frequency pressure into false low-frequency resonance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對採樣頻率與抗混疊設定並比較相鄰壓力感測器的相干性。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「採樣過慢可把高頻壓力錯折成假的低頻共振」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check sample rate and anti-alias filtering and compare coherence between adjacent pressure sensors. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Slow sampling can alias high-frequency pressure into false low-frequency resonance. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以核對採樣頻率與抗混疊設定並比較相鄰壓力感測器的相干性作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對採樣過慢可把高頻壓力錯折成假的低頻共振，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check sample rate and anti-alias filtering and compare coherence between adjacent pressure sensors. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Slow sampling can alias high-frequency pressure into false low-frequency resonance. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「脈動壓力與頻譜」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fluctuating pressure and spectrum\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對採樣頻率與抗混疊設定並比較相鄰壓力感測器的相干性。","最大洪水必定是水躍位置最不利工況"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check sample rate and anti-alias filtering and compare coherence between adjacent pressure sensors.","The largest flood is always the worst jump-location condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對採樣頻率與抗混疊設定並比較相鄰壓力感測器的相干性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check sample rate and anti-alias filtering and compare coherence between adjacent pressure sensors. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b244-v15-32","title":"脈動壓力與頻譜：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fluctuating pressure and spectrum: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「脈動壓力與頻譜」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fluctuating pressure and spectrum” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"採樣過慢可把高頻壓力錯折成假的低頻共振。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對採樣頻率與抗混疊設定並比較相鄰壓力感測器的相干性，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Slow sampling can alias high-frequency pressure into false low-frequency resonance. Diagnose it by the following check: Check sample rate and anti-alias filtering and compare coherence between adjacent pressure sensors. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「壓力均方根就是底板最大設計壓力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Root-mean-square pressure equals the maximum slab design pressure\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"採樣過慢可把高頻壓力錯折成假的低頻共振。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對採樣頻率與抗混疊設定並比較相鄰壓力感測器的相干性，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Slow sampling can alias high-frequency pressure into false low-frequency resonance. Diagnose it by the following check: Check sample rate and anti-alias filtering and compare coherence between adjacent pressure sensors. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「脈動壓力與頻譜」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fluctuating pressure and spectrum\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","池內殘留砂礫少就表示磨耗可以忽略","採樣過慢可把高頻壓力錯折成假的低頻共振。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Little retained sediment means abrasion can be ignored","Slow sampling can alias high-frequency pressure into false low-frequency resonance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"採樣過慢可把高頻壓力錯折成假的低頻共振。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Slow sampling can alias high-frequency pressure into false low-frequency resonance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b244-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「滯留砂礫與磨耗」與「模型比例與尺度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Retained sediment and abrasion\" and \"Model ratios and scale effects\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b244-v15-33","title":"滯留砂礫與磨耗：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Retained sediment and abrasion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「滯留砂礫與磨耗」如何影響溢洪道消能池的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Retained sediment and abrasion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stilling basins for spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"池內回流可反覆搬運砂礫，使磨耗集中於底板與角隅，即使總體能量消散良好也會損傷表面。質量盤點能辨認材料是否滯留，但磨耗速率還受硬度、粒徑與接觸速度控制；需將清淤前後地形與實際磨耗深度聯合分析。 驗證時應重測池底高程與砂礫粒徑並核對清淤稱重紀錄，並辨識以下失效情境：反覆滾動的少量硬礫也可能造成嚴重局部磨坑。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「滯留砂礫與磨耗」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Recirculation can repeatedly move gravel against slabs and corners even when overall dissipation is effective. A mass balance identifies retention but does not determine abrasion rate, which also depends on hardness, size and contact velocity. Compare precleaning and postcleaning bathymetry with measured surface loss. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Resurvey basin elevations and sediment sizes and reconcile weighed cleaning records. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A small quantity of repeatedly circulating hard gravel can excavate deep local pits. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Retained sediment and abrasion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：IncomingSediment=18 t; outgoingSediment=11 t; removedByCleaning=2 t; retainedIncrease=18-11-2=5 t。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: IncomingSediment=18 t; outgoingSediment=11 t; removedByCleaning=2 t; retainedIncrease=18-11-2=5 t.","failure":"常見誤解：「池內殘留砂礫少就表示磨耗可以忽略」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Little retained sediment means abrasion can be ignored\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「滯留砂礫與磨耗」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Retained sediment and abrasion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-33-k1","title":"滯留砂礫與磨耗","titleEn":"Retained sediment and abrasion","text":"池內回流可反覆搬運砂礫，使磨耗集中於底板與角隅，即使總體能量消散良好也會損傷表面。質量盤點能辨認材料是否滯留，但磨耗速率還受硬度、粒徑與接觸速度控制；需將清淤前後地形與實際磨耗深度聯合分析。","textEn":"Recirculation can repeatedly move gravel against slabs and corners even when overall dissipation is effective. A mass balance identifies retention but does not determine abrasion rate, which also depends on hardness, size and contact velocity.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：池內殘留砂礫少就表示磨耗可以忽略 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Little retained sediment means abrasion can be ignored Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「滯留砂礫與磨耗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Retained sediment and abrasion\" is correct?","options":["池內回流可反覆搬運砂礫，使磨耗集中於底板與角隅，即使總體能量消散良好也會損傷表面。","池內殘留砂礫少就表示磨耗可以忽略","福祿相似保證所有物理效應完全相似"],"optionsEn":["Recirculation can repeatedly move gravel against slabs and corners even when overall dissipation is effective.","Little retained sediment means abrasion can be ignored","Froude similarity guarantees similarity of every physical effect"],"answer":0,"explanation":"池內回流可反覆搬運砂礫，使磨耗集中於底板與角隅，即使總體能量消散良好也會損傷表面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Recirculation can repeatedly move gravel against slabs and corners even when overall dissipation is effective. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b244-v15-34","title":"滯留砂礫與磨耗：定量估算","titleEn":"Retained sediment and abrasion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「滯留砂礫與磨耗」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Retained sediment and abrasion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：IncomingSediment=18 t; outgoingSediment=11 t; removedByCleaning=2 t; retainedIncrease=18-11-2=5 t。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: IncomingSediment=18 t; outgoingSediment=11 t; removedByCleaning=2 t; retainedIncrease=18-11-2=5 t. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：重測池底高程與砂礫粒徑並核對清淤稱重紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Resurvey basin elevations and sediment sizes and reconcile weighed cleaning records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：IncomingSediment=18 t; outgoingSediment=11 t; removedByCleaning=2 t; retainedIncrease=18-11-2=5 t。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: IncomingSediment=18 t; outgoingSediment=11 t; removedByCleaning=2 t; retainedIncrease=18-11-2=5 t. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「滯留砂礫與磨耗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Retained sediment and abrasion\", which statement holds?","options":["福祿數相同就保證全部局部壓力相同","原創教學假設：IncomingSediment=18 t; outgoingSediment=11 t; removedByCleaning=2 t; retainedIncrease=18-11-2=5 t。","消散的機械能會自動變成可利用電力"],"optionsEn":["Equal Froude numbers guarantee equal local pressures everywhere","Original teaching assumptions: IncomingSediment=18 t; outgoingSediment=11 t; removedByCleaning=2 t; retainedIncrease=18-11-2=5 t.","Dissipated mechanical energy automatically becomes usable electrical power"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：IncomingSediment=18 t; outgoingSediment=11 t; removedByCleaning=2 t; retainedIncrease=18-11-2=5 t。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: IncomingSediment=18 t; outgoingSediment=11 t; removedByCleaning=2 t; retainedIncrease=18-11-2=5 t. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b244-v15-35","title":"滯留砂礫與磨耗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Retained sediment and abrasion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「滯留砂礫與磨耗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Retained sediment and abrasion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"重測池底高程與砂礫粒徑並核對清淤稱重紀錄。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「反覆滾動的少量硬礫也可能造成嚴重局部磨坑」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Resurvey basin elevations and sediment sizes and reconcile weighed cleaning records. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A small quantity of repeatedly circulating hard gravel can excavate deep local pits. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以重測池底高程與砂礫粒徑並核對清淤稱重紀錄作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對反覆滾動的少量硬礫也可能造成嚴重局部磨坑，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Resurvey basin elevations and sediment sizes and reconcile weighed cleaning records. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A small quantity of repeatedly circulating hard gravel can excavate deep local pits. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：反覆滾動的少量硬礫也可能造成嚴重局部磨坑。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A small quantity of repeatedly circulating hard gravel can excavate deep local pits. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"重測池底高程與砂礫粒徑並核對清淤稱重紀錄。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「反覆滾動的少量硬礫也可能造成嚴重局部磨坑」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Resurvey basin elevations and sediment sizes and reconcile weighed cleaning records. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: A small quantity of repeatedly circulating hard gravel can excavate deep local pits. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以重測池底高程與砂礫粒徑並核對清淤稱重紀錄作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對反覆滾動的少量硬礫也可能造成嚴重局部磨坑，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Resurvey basin elevations and sediment sizes and reconcile weighed cleaning records. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: A small quantity of repeatedly circulating hard gravel can excavate deep local pits. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「滯留砂礫與磨耗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Retained sediment and abrasion\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","平均揚壓合格就排除了瞬時掀板風險","重測池底高程與砂礫粒徑並核對清淤稱重紀錄。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Acceptable mean uplift eliminates transient slab-lifting risk","Resurvey basin elevations and sediment sizes and reconcile weighed cleaning records."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重測池底高程與砂礫粒徑並核對清淤稱重紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Resurvey basin elevations and sediment sizes and reconcile weighed cleaning records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b244-v15-36","title":"滯留砂礫與磨耗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Retained sediment and abrasion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「滯留砂礫與磨耗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Retained sediment and abrasion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"反覆滾動的少量硬礫也可能造成嚴重局部磨坑。診斷時應採取以下查核：重測池底高程與砂礫粒徑並核對清淤稱重紀錄，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A small quantity of repeatedly circulating hard gravel can excavate deep local pits. Diagnose it by the following check: Resurvey basin elevations and sediment sizes and reconcile weighed cleaning records. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「池內殘留砂礫少就表示磨耗可以忽略」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Little retained sediment means abrasion can be ignored\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"反覆滾動的少量硬礫也可能造成嚴重局部磨坑。診斷時應採取以下查核：重測池底高程與砂礫粒徑並核對清淤稱重紀錄，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"A small quantity of repeatedly circulating hard gravel can excavate deep local pits. Diagnose it by the following check: Resurvey basin elevations and sediment sizes and reconcile weighed cleaning records. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「滯留砂礫與磨耗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Retained sediment and abrasion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["反覆滾動的少量硬礫也可能造成嚴重局部磨坑。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","福祿相似保證所有物理效應完全相似"],"optionsEn":["A small quantity of repeatedly circulating hard gravel can excavate deep local pits.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Froude similarity guarantees similarity of every physical effect"],"answer":0,"explanation":"反覆滾動的少量硬礫也可能造成嚴重局部磨坑。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A small quantity of repeatedly circulating hard gravel can excavate deep local pits. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b244-v15-37","title":"模型比例與尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Model ratios and scale effects: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「模型比例與尺度」如何影響溢洪道消能池的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Model ratios and scale effects” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Stilling basins for spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"重力主導的水躍通常採福祿相似，使速度比例為長度比平方根，流量比為長度比的二分之五次方。黏性、表面張力與含氣粒徑無法同時完全相似；模型流量正確不保證氣泡與局部脈壓已等比例重現。 驗證時應核對模型雷諾數與表面張力影響並以不同尺度重複關鍵工況，並辨識以下失效情境：過小模型可能壓低含氣量並扭曲壓力波動。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「模型比例與尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Gravity-dominated jumps commonly use Froude similarity, with velocity scaling as the square root of length and discharge as length to the five-halves power. Viscosity, surface tension and bubble size cannot all be matched simultaneously. Correct discharge scaling does not guarantee reproduction of aeration or local pressure fluctuations. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check model Reynolds and surface-tension effects and repeat critical cases at another scale. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: An excessively small model can suppress aeration and distort pressure fluctuations. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Model ratios and scale effects” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Prototype/model lengthRatio=25; prototypeQ=500 m3/s; modelQ=500/25**2.5=0.160 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Prototype/model lengthRatio=25; prototypeQ=500 m3/s; modelQ=500/25**2.5=0.160 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「福祿相似保證所有物理效應完全相似」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Froude similarity guarantees similarity of every physical effect\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「模型比例與尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Model ratios and scale effects”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-37-k1","title":"模型比例與尺度","titleEn":"Model ratios and scale effects","text":"重力主導的水躍通常採福祿相似，使速度比例為長度比平方根，流量比為長度比的二分之五次方。黏性、表面張力與含氣粒徑無法同時完全相似；模型流量正確不保證氣泡與局部脈壓已等比例重現。","textEn":"Gravity-dominated jumps commonly use Froude similarity, with velocity scaling as the square root of length and discharge as length to the five-halves power. Viscosity, surface tension and bubble size cannot all be matched simultaneously.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：福祿相似保證所有物理效應完全相似 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Froude similarity guarantees similarity of every physical effect Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模型比例與尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Model ratios and scale effects\" is correct?","options":["福祿相似保證所有物理效應完全相似","重力主導的水躍通常採福祿相似，使速度比例為長度比平方根，流量比為長度比的二分之五次方。","平均流速可以當作整個消能池最大流速"],"optionsEn":["Froude similarity guarantees similarity of every physical effect","Gravity-dominated jumps commonly use Froude similarity, with velocity scaling as the square root of length and discharge as length to the five-halves power.","Mean velocity represents the maximum velocity throughout the basin"],"answer":1,"explanation":"重力主導的水躍通常採福祿相似，使速度比例為長度比平方根，流量比為長度比的二分之五次方。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Gravity-dominated jumps commonly use Froude similarity, with velocity scaling as the square root of length and discharge as length to the five-halves power. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b244-v15-38","title":"模型比例與尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Model ratios and scale effects: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「模型比例與尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Model ratios and scale effects” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Prototype/model lengthRatio=25; prototypeQ=500 m3/s; modelQ=500/25**2.5=0.160 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Prototype/model lengthRatio=25; prototypeQ=500 m3/s; modelQ=500/25**2.5=0.160 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對模型雷諾數與表面張力影響並以不同尺度重複關鍵工況。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check model Reynolds and surface-tension effects and repeat critical cases at another scale.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Prototype/model lengthRatio=25; prototypeQ=500 m3/s; modelQ=500/25**2.5=0.160 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Prototype/model lengthRatio=25; prototypeQ=500 m3/s; modelQ=500/25**2.5=0.160 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模型比例與尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Model ratios and scale effects\", which statement holds?","options":["水躍前後可用機械能相等直接求水深","最大洪水必定是水躍位置最不利工況","原創教學假設：Prototype/model lengthRatio=25; prototypeQ=500 m3/s; modelQ=500/25**2.5=0.160 m3/s。"],"optionsEn":["Equal mechanical energy determines depths across a hydraulic jump","The largest flood is always the worst jump-location condition","Original teaching assumptions: Prototype/model lengthRatio=25; prototypeQ=500 m3/s; modelQ=500/25**2.5=0.160 m3/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Prototype/model lengthRatio=25; prototypeQ=500 m3/s; modelQ=500/25**2.5=0.160 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Prototype/model lengthRatio=25; prototypeQ=500 m3/s; modelQ=500/25**2.5=0.160 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b244-v15-39","title":"模型比例與尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Model ratios and scale effects: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「模型比例與尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Model ratios and scale effects” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對模型雷諾數與表面張力影響並以不同尺度重複關鍵工況。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「過小模型可能壓低含氣量並扭曲壓力波動」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check model Reynolds and surface-tension effects and repeat critical cases at another scale. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An excessively small model can suppress aeration and distort pressure fluctuations. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以核對模型雷諾數與表面張力影響並以不同尺度重複關鍵工況作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對過小模型可能壓低含氣量並扭曲壓力波動，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check model Reynolds and surface-tension effects and repeat critical cases at another scale. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An excessively small model can suppress aeration and distort pressure fluctuations. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：過小模型可能壓低含氣量並扭曲壓力波動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An excessively small model can suppress aeration and distort pressure fluctuations. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對模型雷諾數與表面張力影響並以不同尺度重複關鍵工況。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「過小模型可能壓低含氣量並扭曲壓力波動」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check model Reynolds and surface-tension effects and repeat critical cases at another scale. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: An excessively small model can suppress aeration and distort pressure fluctuations. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以核對模型雷諾數與表面張力影響並以不同尺度重複關鍵工況作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對過小模型可能壓低含氣量並扭曲壓力波動，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check model Reynolds and surface-tension effects and repeat critical cases at another scale. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: An excessively small model can suppress aeration and distort pressure fluctuations. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模型比例與尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Model ratios and scale effects\"?","options":["核對模型雷諾數與表面張力影響並以不同尺度重複關鍵工況。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","總動量平均分攤就代表每個墩塊受力相同"],"optionsEn":["Check model Reynolds and surface-tension effects and repeat critical cases at another scale.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Averaging total momentum proves equal force on every baffle"],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對模型雷諾數與表面張力影響並以不同尺度重複關鍵工況。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check model Reynolds and surface-tension effects and repeat critical cases at another scale. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b244-v15-40","title":"模型比例與尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Model ratios and scale effects: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b244-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「模型比例與尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Model ratios and scale effects” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"過小模型可能壓低含氣量並扭曲壓力波動。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對模型雷諾數與表面張力影響並以不同尺度重複關鍵工況，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An excessively small model can suppress aeration and distort pressure fluctuations. Diagnose it by the following check: Check model Reynolds and surface-tension effects and repeat critical cases at another scale. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「福祿相似保證所有物理效應完全相似」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Froude similarity guarantees similarity of every physical effect\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b244-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"過小模型可能壓低含氣量並扭曲壓力波動。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對模型雷諾數與表面張力影響並以不同尺度重複關鍵工況，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"An excessively small model can suppress aeration and distort pressure fluctuations. Diagnose it by the following check: Check model Reynolds and surface-tension effects and repeat critical cases at another scale. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b244-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模型比例與尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Model ratios and scale effects\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","過小模型可能壓低含氣量並扭曲壓力波動。","平均流速可以當作整個消能池最大流速"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An excessively small model can suppress aeration and distort pressure fluctuations.","Mean velocity represents the maximum velocity throughout the basin"],"answer":1,"explanation":"過小模型可能壓低含氣量並扭曲壓力波動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An excessively small model can suppress aeration and distort pressure fluctuations. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-hoover-owner","v15s-glen-owner"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
